            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0343" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2779: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-12T22:00:00-04:00">January 12, 1933—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 12—9:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. The Bolivian Government today replied to the Chilean suggestion as follows:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We thank the Chilean Minister for Foreign Affairs for his solicitous
                            intervention in sending us a project of a proposal for the settlement
                                <pb facs="0344" n="256" xml:id="pg256"/> of the controversy between
                            Bolivia and Paraguay. But we suggest for many obvious reasons the
                            necessity of reviving the proposal of the five neutrals of December
                                15<anchor n="36" xml:id="d168-f1"/> which would now be signed by the
                            four neighbors as well.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
